WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:04.282
In this video, you will learn how to run voting once it has started.

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:09.608
You will pause and resume it, check the results, and remove a vote that should not count.

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:10.586
We start on the map.

00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:13.235
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:16.174 --> 00:00:18.724
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:21.522
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:27.723
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:27.723 --> 00:00:30.505
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:30.505 --> 00:00:35.068
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:35.769
Tap it.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.297
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:45.939
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:45.939 --> 00:00:47.821
Tap Mine, your personal page.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.483
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:53.272 --> 00:00:56.877
This card is where you control the contest while it is running.

00:00:56.877 --> 00:01:00.362
Voting opens and closes on your dates by itself.

00:01:00.362 --> 00:01:03.073
The Controls card lets you step in when you need to.

00:01:03.932 --> 00:01:07.790
The last row, Contest page, has an Unpublish button.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.920
It hides the whole contest from the public, and you can publish it again.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.459
The next video shows how.

00:01:14.325 --> 00:01:17.827
Say you spot something odd, or you need to fix a mistake.

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:22.024
Tap Pause voting, and votes stop right away, until you say otherwise.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:27.213
When you are ready, tap Resume voting, and voting carries on.

00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:30.136
Now tap Results.

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:35.308
Here is the full tally, category by category.

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:41.342
You can always see the counts, even when you have hidden them from the public so people are not swayed by who is ahead.

00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:44.445
Open Review individual votes.

00:01:44.445 --> 00:01:47.983
Every single vote is listed, with when it was cast.

00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:53.933
The system flags odd patterns, like a burst of votes within a few seconds, so you can look more closely.

00:01:55.646 --> 00:01:58.243
If a vote should not count, tap Void next to it.

00:01:59.887 --> 00:02:04.631
It is removed from the tally, and you can restore it later if you change your mind.

00:02:04.631 --> 00:02:06.281
This keeps the contest fair.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.521
Next up: Unpublish and publish again.
